From: l16-linux
Subject: [PATCH] gstreamer: Apply controls to requests that are queued

The pending controls were applied (and cleared) before the request got its
buffers; when the pool had none free, the request was dropped and the controls
with it, so most controls set while streaming were lost. Apply them once the
buffers are attached, under the object lock set_property() changes them under.
---
diff -ruN a2/src/gstreamer/gstlibcamerasrc.cpp b2/src/gstreamer/gstlibcamerasrc.cpp
--- a/src/gstreamer/gstlibcamerasrc.cpp	2026-09-29 23:29:03.265857649 -0700
+++ b/src/gstreamer/gstlibcamerasrc.cpp	2026-09-29 23:35:23.522893684 -0700
@@ -185,9 +185,6 @@
 	if (!request)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
-	/* Apply controls */
-	controls_.applyControls(request);
-
 	std::unique_ptr<RequestWrap> wrap =
 		std::make_unique<RequestWrap>(std::move(request));
 
@@ -209,6 +206,17 @@
 		wrap->attachBuffer(srcpad, buffer);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Apply controls, now that the request will be queued: applied before
+	 * the buffers were found, they were cleared and then dropped with the
+	 * request whenever the pool had no free buffer. set_property() changes
+	 * them under the object lock, from the application thread.
+	 */
+	{
+		GLibLocker locker(GST_OBJECT(src_));
+		controls_.applyControls(wrap->request_);
+	}
+
 	GST_TRACE_OBJECT(src_, "Requesting buffers");
 
 	{
